  "summary": "Read synthesis.tex independently, then checked the expansive study against the cited Missal, Lasance/Walsh, Augustine, Bellarmine, Chrysostom, Jerome, Aquinas, Bede, Theophylact and Fromage loci. The interpretations distinguish deliverance already begun from the final rescue still awaited and explain how God changes those who pray with confidence. Inspected all ten pages of the selected native host-pdfTeX synthesis (SHA-256 2dfed600e8530e1dc4a571cf0e29f49f77d212f85317ca65557e2411115979ac) and checked the settled page markers. Page 1 has eleven appointments and four sense rows, page 2 alone locates Matthew 24:15\u201335 at Mount Olivet where Jesus foretells Jerusalem\u2019s ruin and his coming, and its derived A.D. 29 event date is readily distinguished from both composition rows. Commentary starts on page 5. The underdeveloped themes pages and the lost qualification about the timing and form of help in prayer require revision."
}
